# Wrapper scopes for `SaraIncome`

> Module SaraIncomeWrappers

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraIncome as Src

Generated by `cutecat_scripts/generate_dataset.py`; edits are
overwritten. Each scope below adds no rule: it declares one input
per parameter of a top-level function of the port and returns what
that function returns. CUTECat explores one entry point per run,
and a top-level function is not one until something names it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FnEventContribution:
  input ev content W.Event
  input y content integer
  output result content money

declaration scope FnEveryoneIncome:
  input world content W.World
  input y content integer
  output result content money

declaration scope FnRoleCount:
  input l content list of W.Entity
  input e content W.Entity
  output result content integer

```

```catala
scope FnEventContribution:
  definition result equals Src.event_contribution of ev, y

scope FnEveryoneIncome:
  definition result equals Src.everyone_income of world, y

scope FnRoleCount:
  definition result equals Src.role_count of l, e

```
